> create bucket Photos { type: hash, Comments fifoStore, Shots blobStore }
OK  created bucket app.Photos (type hash, whole)
Stores: 2 store field(s) declared
> describe bucket Photos
BUCKET app.Photos
---
Type:               hash
Entries:            0
Logical size:       0 B (before compression and compaction)
Encrypted:          no (this node's store)
Replication factor: 1 (inherited)
Placement:          whole
Indexes:            (none — declare them when you create the bucket)
Stores:             (elements summed over every document)
  Comments     fifoStore  0 element(s)
  Shots        blobStore  0 element(s)
> create bucket Plain { type: hash, Caption string }
OK  created bucket app.Plain (type hash, whole)
note: field types on scalar fields (Caption string) are not enforced in this release; only store fields are created.
